    },
    "body": "The expert review P1 ran over four rows differing only in the value inside turn 1, scoring existing checkpoints with no training and classifying each failure. In arm-as the model own turn 1 is Noted. and its turn-2 reply is Noted. (cats2) or I see. (cats5) - a register loop the mixture created, since those are the hard-coded turn-1 answers of every family in that generator. In arm-t2 the ana row replies My name is Ana brain., retrieving the value and still failing to answer - the readout failure downstream of retrieval the review predicted. That supports the leading mechanism and explains why every store improvement failed: rounds 134, 136 and 143 each kept or reintroduced the acknowledgement register, so each taught the same loop. The next data change is named: turn-1 answers must be short content-bearing copies of the premise. The pinned conditions and DELTA margins are still running. References #820",
